  "definition": "observed = max distance from the nearest ignition among each overpass's detections (times are upper bounds); model = max distance from the nearest ignition among cells the calibrated baseline reached by that hour"
 },
 "notes": "dead_moisture_pct is the 1-h value; 10-h = +1, 100-h = +2 points; live moisture fixed at baseline. The baseline's dead moisture is hourly (1-h 7.3\u201326.8 %, median 16.5 %; `moisture.hourly`), so the baseline dead_moisture_pct is only the what-if starting value. Grid runs use a constant wind; the baseline uses the hourly MERRA-2 wind. Surface fire only: no crowning, spotting, suppression or fire\u2013atmosphere feedback. Fuels from 500 m MODIS land cover through a coarse IGBP\u2192Anderson crosswalk (the largest error source). Single-point MERRA-2 wind (~50 km grid) over steep terrain. Baseline dead fuel moisture follows MERRA-2 humidity hour by hour (time-lag model); what-if runs use a constant scenario value. Hotspot times are upper bounds limited by the overpass frequency. Counterfactuals and absolute timings are illustrative; differences between runs are more reliable than absolute arrival times.",
 "prep_notes": [
  "Grid: EPSG:32613, 556\u00d7556 at 90 m, lon/lat bounds [-106.3131, 55.8533, -105.4584, 56.3486]",
